+## Service principal
+
+The runtime keeps each tenant in its own SQLite file (Rust) or Durable Object
+(Cloudflare), so the bridge has no database to write. A released app's post to
+a board whose Boards powerup is disabled (`boards.createMessage` fails with
+`Boards powerup is disabled for this tenant`) is written by the internal
+Reducer `legacyBridge.createBoardMessage` instead, called on a service socket
+(Gonvex `docs/service-principals.md`). The bridge first checks, through the
+member's own session, that the board exists and that the member may publish
+to it; the Reducer checks both again in its transaction. The message id and
+the runtime idempotency key derive from the phone's write intent, so a retry
+or a bridge restart after commit creates one post.
+
+Create a credential and configure the runtime with its digest:
+
+```bash
+token="gvx_svc_$(openssl rand -hex 32)"
+printf %s "$token" | sha256sum
+```
+
+```json
+[{"id":"whagons-legacy-bridge","tokenSha256":"<hex>","projects":["<project>"],
+  "functions":["legacyBridge.createBoardMessage"]}]
+```
+
+Add that entry to the runtime's `GONVEX_SERVICE_PRINCIPALS` and set
+`LEGACY_BRIDGE_SERVICE_TOKEN=$token` on the bridge. The id must be
+`whagons-legacy-bridge`: the Reducer refuses every other caller. Without the
+token the fallback fails closed with
+`legacy board message service principal is not configured`.
+`LEGACY_BRIDGE_DATABASE_URL` and `LEGACY_BRIDGE_TENANT_DATABASE` are no longer
+read; a set `LEGACY_BRIDGE_DATABASE_URL` only logs that it is ignored.
+
 ## Project and tenant aliases
 
 Phones send the project id compiled into their build. Released 5.1.31+
